From: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Date: Thu, 05 Nov 2026 17:38:33 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: track optional firmware DMA and MLO borrowers

Backport the complete optional firmware memory allocator from
b4f7857f9c0c21e83d0c3e76917093f4011053db, including its fixed PCI
assignment path. Retain 317 named-memory/AFC and 342 host-DDR offsets.
Keep coherent allocation ownership separate from fixed mappings and MLO
views; prune buffers omitted by a shorter recovery request and use one
referenced-device pool for the complete shared MLO request.

Local adjustment: count each device holding a successfully assigned MLO
view independently of core_start. A partner can already consume a QMI
memory response before num_started increments, so a failed request on a
different partner must not release that pool. Repeated requests replace
only their own view reference, reuse an equal-sized pool, and may resize
a pool only after the last borrower and started core have left. All
references and ownership transitions are protected by the group mutex.
Also release a coherent owner before clearing an unknown fixed-PCI type.

This changes host allocation ownership, not firmware memory mode, ring
sizes, reserved-memory policy or the HW1 non-MLO policy.

Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
